From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 08 Oct 2026 06:32:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: raise the beacon loss limit to 40 intervals

The driver monitors beacons for a station link itself. It reports
beacon loss after 7 missed beacon intervals, about 0.7 s at 100 TU.
mac80211 does not run its own beacon timer for a driver that monitors
the connection. Thus the raised mac80211 beacon loss count of this
build has no effect on a chip that uses the driver monitor.

A station link now reports beacon loss after 40 missed beacon
intervals, about 4 s at 100 TU. The limit matches the beacon loss
count that the local mac80211 package sets. A station link then has
the same tolerance whether mac80211 or the driver monitors beacons.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt76.h |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt76.h
+++ b/mt76.h
@@ -425,7 +425,7 @@ enum mt76_wcid_flags {
 };
 
 #define MT76_N_WCIDS 1088
-#define MT76_BEACON_MON_MAX_MISS	7
+#define MT76_BEACON_MON_MAX_MISS	40
 
 /* stored in ieee80211_tx_info::hw_queue */
 #define MT_TX_HW_QUEUE_PHY		GENMASK(3, 2)
